   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5c675d41",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Series sinteticas de log-retorno com GARCH(1,1)\n",
    "\n",
    "Como complemento ao restante do notebook, esta secao usa um modelo\n",
    "GARCH(1,1) para gerar series sinteticas de log-retorno a partir dos\n",
    "mesmos dados reais do ativo ja coletados anteriormente (`price_tensor`\n",
    "e `return_values`), sem a necessidade de baixar a serie novamente.\n",
    "\n",
    "O objetivo e diferente da deteccao de outliers feita acima: em vez de\n",
    "identificar anomalias na serie real, ajustamos um modelo GARCH(1,1)\n",
    "com residuos t-Student sobre os log-retornos reais e simulamos\n",
    "multiplas trajetorias futuras que preservam a mesma volatilidade\n",
    "condicional e a mesma cauda pesada estimadas a partir dos dados reais.\n",
    "Essas trajetorias sinteticas nunca ocorreram de fato, mas sao\n",
    "estatisticamente compativeis com o processo estimado."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0039d053",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Instalacao e importacao das bibliotecas do GARCH\n",
    "\n",
    "A celula abaixo instala a biblioteca `arch`, usada para ajustar e\n",
    "simular modelos GARCH, e importa os componentes necessarios para o\n",
    "restante desta secao."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "id": "42d2029f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!uv pip install arch -qqq"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
   "id": "bb189503",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from arch import arch_model\n",
    "from arch.univariate import StudentsT\n",
    "\n",
    "from pgl_utils.deep_learning import plot_real_and_synthetic_continuation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b84005ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Parametros da simulacao\n",
    "\n",
    "As constantes abaixo controlam o horizonte de simulacao (em dias\n",
    "uteis), o numero de trajetorias sinteticas geradas e quantas dessas\n",
    "trajetorias sao efetivamente desenhadas nos graficos. A mesma\n",
    "`RANDOM_SEED` definida no inicio do notebook e reutilizada para\n",
    "garantir reprodutibilidade."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 40,
   "id": "1e71510e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SYNTHETIC_HORIZON_DAYS = 90\n",
    "N_SYNTHETIC_PATHS = 200\n",
    "N_PATHS_TO_PLOT = 30"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dc9484d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Ajuste do modelo GARCH(1,1)\n",
    "\n",
    "A funcao abaixo ajusta um modelo GARCH(1,1) com residuos com\n",
    "distribuicao t-Student sobre a serie de log-retornos, informada em\n",
    "porcentagem (pratica usual ao utilizar a biblioteca `arch`). A semente\n",
    "aleatoria e fixada diretamente na distribuicao dos residuos, pois e\n",
    "esse objeto que controla a aleatoriedade utilizada posteriormente\n",
    "durante a simulacao das trajetorias sinteticas."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 41,
   "id": "d3ba3997",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def fit_garch(\n",
    "    log_returns_pct: np.ndarray,\n",
    "    random_seed: int,\n",
    "):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Fit a GARCH(1,1) model with Student's t errors.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        log_returns_pct: One-dimensional array with the log-return\n",
    "            series, expressed in percentage points.\n",
    "        random_seed: Seed used to initialize the random number\n",
    "            generator of the Student's t error distribution, ensuring\n",
    "            that later simulations are reproducible.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        The fitted result object returned by the `arch` library, which\n",
    "        exposes methods such as `.forecast()` and `.summary()`.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    model_specification = arch_model(\n",
    "        log_returns_pct,\n",
    "        mean=\"Constant\",\n",
    "        vol=\"Garch\",\n",
    "        p=1,\n",
    "        q=1,\n",
    "        dist=\"t\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    model_specification.distribution = StudentsT(seed=random_seed)\n",
    "    fitted_result = model_specification.fit(disp=\"off\")\n",
    "    return fitted_result"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 42,
   "id": "993de43a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "garch_result = fit_garch(log_return_tensor.numpy().astype(np.float64) * 100.0, RANDOM_SEED)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b7b7a73b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Simulacao de trajetorias sinteticas de log-retorno\n",
    "\n",
    "A partir do modelo GARCH ajustado, simulamos multiplas trajetorias\n",
    "futuras de log-retorno. Cada trajetoria e gerada respeitando a mesma\n",
    "estrutura de volatilidade condicional e a mesma distribuicao de cauda\n",
    "pesada estimadas a partir dos dados reais."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "4ce53007",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def simulate_synthetic_returns(\n",
    "    garch_result,\n",
    "    horizon_days: int,\n",
    "    n_paths: int,\n",
    ") -> np.ndarray:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Simulate synthetic log-return paths from a fitted GARCH model.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        garch_result: Fitted GARCH result object, as returned by\n",
    "            `fit_garch`.\n",
    "        horizon_days: Number of future days to simulate for each path.\n",
    "        n_paths: Number of independent synthetic paths to simulate.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        A two-dimensional array of shape (n_paths, horizon_days) with\n",
    "        the simulated log-return paths, already converted back from\n",
    "        percentage points to plain log-return units.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    forecast_result = garch_result.forecast(\n",
    "        horizon=horizon_days,\n",
    "        method=\"simulation\",\n",
    "        simulations=n_paths,\n",
    "        reindex=False,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    synthetic_paths_pct = forecast_result.simulations.values[0]\n",
    "    return synthetic_paths_pct / 100.0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 44,
   "id": "6f7f9233",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "C:\\Users\\202303211252\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\ipykernel_38136\\2331308028.py:8: DeprecationWarning: The 'generic' unit for NumPy timedelta is deprecated, and will raise an error in the future. This includes implicit conversion of bare integers (e.g. `+ 1`).Please use a specific unit instead.\n",
      "  start=dates[-1] + pd.Timedelta(days=1),\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "(200, 90)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 44,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "synthetic_returns = simulate_synthetic_returns(\n",
    "    garch_result,\n",
    "    SYNTHETIC_HORIZON_DAYS,\n",
    "    N_SYNTHETIC_PATHS,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "synthetic_dates = pd.bdate_range(\n",
    "    start=dates[-1] + pd.Timedelta(days=1),\n",
    "    periods=SYNTHETIC_HORIZON_DAYS,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "synthetic_returns.shape"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9a775237",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Reconstrucao do preco sintetico\n",
    "\n",
    "Cada trajetoria sintetica de log-retorno pode ser transformada de\n",
    "volta em uma trajetoria de preco, encadeando os retornos a partir do\n",
    "ultimo preco real conhecido: `P_sintetico[t+1] = P[t] * exp(r[t+1])`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 45,
   "id": "6cd61435",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def reconstruct_price_paths(\n",
    "    last_known_price: float,\n",
    "    synthetic_returns: np.ndarray,\n",
    ") -> np.ndarray:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Reconstruct synthetic price paths from simulated log-returns.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        last_known_price: Last observed real price, used as the\n",
    "            starting point for every reconstructed path.\n",
    "        synthetic_returns: Two-dimensional array of shape\n",
    "            (n_paths, horizon_days) with the simulated log-return\n",
    "            paths.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        A two-dimensional array with the same shape as\n",
    "        `synthetic_returns`, containing the reconstructed synthetic\n",
    "        price paths.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    cumulative_log_return = np.cumsum(synthetic_returns, axis=1)\n",
    "    return last_known_price * np.exp(cumulative_log_return)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "id": "49fe3dff",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "last_known_price = price_values[-1]\n",
    "synthetic_prices = reconstruct_price_paths(last_known_price, synthetic_returns)\n",
    "\n",
    "mean_synthetic_return_path = synthetic_returns.mean(axis=0)\n",
    "mean_synthetic_price_path = synthetic_prices.mean(axis=0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "42b5e408",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Visualizacao: serie real seguida da continuacao sintetica\n",
    "\n",
    "`plot_real_and_synthetic_continuation` (importada de\n",
    "`pgl_utils.deep_learning`) retorna tres graficos:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Um grafico combinado, em dois paineis (log-retorno e preco), com a\n",
    "   serie real seguida de todas as trajetorias sinteticas simuladas\n",
    "   sobrepostas e sua media.\n",
    "2. Um grid com uma trajetoria sintetica de log-retorno por painel,\n",
    "   cada uma precedida pelos ultimos `tail_real_days_for_grid` dias da\n",
    "   serie real (por padrao, os ultimos 30 dias, para simplificar o\n",
    "   grafico).\n",
    "3. O mesmo grid, para os precos sinteticos reconstruidos."
   ]
  },
