   "source": [
    "## Avaliacao de pontos de compra e venda nas series sinteticas (GARCH)\n",
    "\n",
    "Nesta secao, reaproveitamos o autoencoder `dense_model`, ja treinado\n",
    "sobre os log-retornos reais, e o `signal_generator`\n",
    "(`TradingSignalGenerator`) definido anteriormente, para avaliar os\n",
    "pontos de compra e venda diretamente sobre as `N_SYNTHETIC_PATHS`\n",
    "trajetorias sinteticas geradas pelo GARCH(1,1). Nenhum modelo e\n",
    "retreinado: o mesmo autoencoder e o mesmo limiar de anomalia\n",
    "(`anomaly_threshold`), aprendidos a partir dos dados reais, sao\n",
    "aplicados as series sinteticas."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e37f1352",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Normalizacao das series sinteticas\n",
    "\n",
    "Os log-retornos sinteticos sao normalizados com a mesma media e desvio\n",
    "padrao do conjunto de treino real (`return_train_mean` e\n",
    "`return_train_std`), evitando qualquer vazamento de informacao e\n",
    "garantindo que o autoencoder receba entradas na mesma escala usada\n",
    "durante o treinamento."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 48,
   "id": "a124ea74",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "synthetic_returns_tensor = torch.from_numpy(synthetic_returns.astype(np.float32))\n",
    "normalized_synthetic_returns_tensor, _, _ = normalize_series(\n",
    "    synthetic_returns_tensor,\n",
    "    mean=return_train_mean,\n",
    "    std=return_train_std,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "72895319",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Construcao das janelas deslizantes por trajetoria sintetica\n",
    "\n",
    "Cada uma das `N_SYNTHETIC_PATHS` trajetorias sinteticas e tratada de\n",
    "forma independente: a funcao abaixo constroi, para cada trajetoria,\n",
    "todas as janelas deslizantes de tamanho `WINDOW_SIZE`, da mesma forma\n",
    "que foi feito para a serie real, mas de uma vez para o lote inteiro de\n",
    "trajetorias."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 49,
   "id": "2b5774f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def build_sliding_windows(\n",
    "    series_values: np.ndarray,\n",
    "    window_size: int,\n",
    ") -> np.ndarray:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Build sliding windows along the last axis of a batch of series.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        series_values: Array of shape (n_series, horizon_days) with\n",
    "            one or more time series.\n",
    "        window_size: Number of consecutive time steps contained in\n",
    "            each window.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        An array of shape (n_series, horizon_days - window_size + 1,\n",
    "        window_size) with every sliding window of each series.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return np.lib.stride_tricks.sliding_window_view(\n",
    "        series_values, window_shape=window_size, axis=1,\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 50,
   "id": "7d66aeea",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "torch.Size([16200, 10])"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 50,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "synthetic_windows = build_sliding_windows(\n",
    "    normalized_synthetic_returns_tensor.numpy(), WINDOW_SIZE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "n_synthetic_paths, n_windows_per_path, _ = synthetic_windows.shape\n",
    "\n",
    "synthetic_windows_tensor = torch.from_numpy(\n",
    "    synthetic_windows.reshape(-1, WINDOW_SIZE)\n",
    ").to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "synthetic_windows_tensor.shape"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1cc95203",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Erro de reconstrucao e deteccao de outliers nas series sinteticas\n",
    "\n",
    "O erro de reconstrucao de cada janela sintetica e calculado com a\n",
    "mesma funcao `compute_reconstruction_scores` usada para a serie real.\n",
    "Para manter a mesma nocao de anomalia aprendida pelo autoencoder,\n",
    "reaproveitamos o `anomaly_threshold` ja calculado a partir dos dados\n",
    "reais, em vez de recalcular um novo limiar especificamente para as\n",
    "series sinteticas."
   ]
  },
